cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use omnibias in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "omnibias: numerically-stable closed-form n-th derivative forward-pass framework"
abstract: >-
  omnibias provides closed-form activation derivatives and Taylor-jet
  propagation for supported neural networks, avoiding nested spatial
  automatic differentiation while retaining parameter gradients. PyTorch,
  JAX and Keras implementations share a pure-Python coefficient core.
  Directional and multivariate jets compose activation derivatives through
  Bell / Faa di Bruno combinatorics. Field operators, soft partitions and
  scoped verified numerics support physics-informed neural network workflows.
  Accuracy and performance depend on order, dtype, architecture and backend.
type: software
